---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Airbrush Learn"
  description="Privacy policy for Airbrush Learn, a SprayGunner property."
  canonicalPath="/privacy-policy"
>
  <div class="pt-10 pb-16 mx-auto max-w-wide px-5">
    <div class="prose prose-site max-w-prose mx-auto">
      <h1 class="font-serif max-[640px]:text-[1.7rem]">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated: August 23, 2026</em></p>
      <p>
        Airbrush Learn is published by SprayGunner. This page explains what
        information we collect through this site and how it's used.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Gallery submissions.</strong> If you submit artwork through
        our <a href="/gallery/submit">community gallery</a>, we collect the
        title you give it, your name, your email address, and the image file
        itself. Your name and title are shown publicly if your submission is
        approved and published. Your email address is never shown publicly —
        it's used only to reach you if we have a question about your
        submission during review, and it's deleted from our systems once a
        submission is approved or rejected.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Server logs.</strong> Like most websites, our hosting
        provider (Netlify) automatically logs basic request information (IP
        address, browser type, pages requested) for security and reliability
        purposes. We don't use this data for tracking or marketing.
      </p>

      <h2>What we don't currently collect</h2>
      <p>
        We do not currently run analytics or advertising scripts, and we do
        not set tracking cookies. If that changes, we'll update this policy
        to reflect it.
      </p>

      <h2>Published gallery artwork</h2>
      <p>
        Once a gallery submission is approved, the artwork, its title, and
        the name you provided are published on this site and stored in our
        public source code repository — meaning they become part of a
        public, permanent record, including in the site's revision history,
        even if the piece is later removed from display. See our
        <a href="/terms-of-use">Terms of Use</a> for the rights you grant us
        when you submit work.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party links</h2>
      <p>
        Articles and pages on this site link to third-party sites, including
        spraygunner.com and manufacturer or reference sites. We aren't
        responsible for the privacy practices of those sites.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the site changes. The "Last updated"
        date above reflects the most recent revision.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be directed to us through
        <a href="https://spraygunner.com/">spraygunner.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
